    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "id": "beam_calculator",
      "content": "American Standard S Beam Calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "beam_depth",
          "label": "Beam Depth (h)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "in",
          "defaultValue": 12
        },
        {
          "id": "beam_width",
          "label": "Flange Width (w)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "in",
          "defaultValue": 5.477
        },
        {
          "id": "web_thickness",
          "label": "Web Thickness (s)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "in",
          "defaultValue": 0.687
        },
        {
          "id": "sectional_area",
          "label": "Sectional Area",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "in²",
          "defaultValue": 14.7
        },
        {
          "id": "moment_inertia_x",
          "label": "Moment of Inertia - Ix",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "in⁴",
          "defaultValue": 305
        },
        {
          "id": "moment_inertia_y",
          "label": "Moment of Inertia - Iy",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "in⁴",
          "defaultValue": 15.7
        },
        {
          "id": "section_modulus_x",
          "label": "Section Modulus - Sx",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "in³",
          "defaultValue": 50.8
        },
        {
          "id": "section_modulus_y",
          "label": "Section Modulus - Sy",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "in³",
          "defaultValue": 5.74
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "bending_stress_x",
          "label": "Maximum Bending Stress - X axis",
          "formula": "inputs.moment_inertia_x * 1.5 / inputs.section_modulus_x",
          "unit": "lbf/in²",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "bending_stress_y",
          "label": "Maximum Bending Stress - Y axis",
          "formula": "inputs.moment_inertia_y * 1.5 / inputs.section_modulus_y",
          "unit": "lbf/in²",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "radius_gyration_x",
          "label": "Radius of Gyration - rx",
          "formula": "Math.sqrt(inputs.moment_inertia_x / inputs.sectional_area)",
          "unit": "in",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "radius_gyration_y",
          "label": "Radius of Gyration - ry",
          "formula": "Math.sqrt(inputs.moment_inertia_y / inputs.sectional_area)",
          "unit": "in",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "info",
      "content": "## American Standard S Beams (ASTM A6)\n\n### Standard Specifications\n- **Units**: Imperial (inches, pounds)\n- **Cross Section**: I-shaped beam\n- **Standards**: ASTM A6\n\n### Common Applications\n- Building construction\n- Bridge construction\n- Industrial structures\n- Heavy-duty framing\n\n### Beam Designation\nBeams are specified by depth and weight per unit length (e.g., S 12 x 50):\n- **S**: Standard I-beam\n- **12**: Nominal depth in inches\n- **50**: Weight in pounds per foot\n\n### Key Parameters\n- **h**: Depth of the beam\n- **w**: Width of the flange\n- **s**: Web thickness\n- **Ix, Iy**: Moment of inertia about X and Y axes\n- **Sx, Sy**: Section modulus about X and Y axes\n\n### Unit Conversions\n- 1 in³ = 1.64 × 10⁴ mm³ = 16.4 cm³\n- 1 in⁴ = 4.16 × 10⁵ mm⁴ = 41.6 cm⁴"
    }
